#N canvas 0 0 720 640 10;
#X text 12 8 vgm~ - VGM/VGZ player that drives one ym2612~ + one sn76489~;
#X text 12 28 Loads a VGM log (gzip .vgz supported) \, paces it at the VGM's 44100 Hz timebase \, and emits the chip writes per outlet: outlet 0 = `ch<k> reg <addr> <data>` (ch1-3 = chip port A \, ch4-6 = port B \, register bytes verbatim - the ym2612~'s Nuked core is the whole chip \, all six channels \, so a single instance plays everything). Outlet 1 = the PSG chip's raw bytes (feed a sn76489~). Outlet 2 = signal: the YM2612 DAC PCM stream. Outlet 3 = bang at the end of non-looping data.;
#X text 20 190 transport;
#X msg 20 210 load demo.vgm;
#X msg 120 210 play;
#X msg 180 210 pause;
#X msg 240 210 stop;
#X msg 300 210 goto loop;
#X msg 400 210 goto 44100;
#X msg 20 240 loop 1;
#X msg 100 240 loop 0;
#X msg 180 240 info;
#X text 20 280 load resolves the file through the pd search path (the app's bundled bank folder) and the patch's own directory. goto seeks by rescanning with a register shadow \, so the resumed audio keeps its patch state. pause/stop key off all YM channels.;
#X text 20 360 limits: DAC Stream Control (0x90-0x95) is parsed but not played (the common 0x8n DAC path is) \, AY8910 writes are forwarded on outlet 1 (sn76489~ drops them silently) \, compressed data blocks stop the stream \, FM3 special mode runs in normal mode.;
#X text 20 440 wire ONE ym2612~ + ONE sn76489~ (see the vgm-player example):;
#X msg 20 480 raw 1;
#X obj 20 520 vgm~;
#X obj 120 520 ym2612~;
#X obj 120 480 sn76489~;
#X text 200 520 outlet 0 -> ym2612~: ch<k> reg writes \, six channels \, one chip;
#X obj 20 560 *~ 0.2;
#X obj 120 560 dac~;
#X connect 3 0 16 0;
#X connect 4 0 16 0;
#X connect 5 0 16 0;
#X connect 6 0 16 0;
#X connect 7 0 16 0;
#X connect 8 0 16 0;
#X connect 9 0 16 0;
#X connect 10 0 16 0;
#X connect 11 0 16 0;
#X connect 15 0 17 0;
#X connect 16 0 17 0;
#X connect 16 1 18 0;
#X connect 16 2 20 0;
#X connect 17 0 20 0;
#X connect 18 0 20 0;
#X connect 20 0 21 0;
#X connect 20 0 21 1;
#X text 200 545 per-channel signal outlets: ym2612~ 1..6 = chip channels \, sn76489~ 1..4 = tone 1-3 / noise (outlet 0 of each = the sum);
